  "readerProfile": "An industry-oriented ML PhD student (Tübingen) working on multimodal medical AI for precision medicine, with a background in agent-based clinical systems and clinical data harmonization. Core interests: (1) multimodal representation learning that fuses heterogeneous patient data — clinical history/EHR, labs and biomarkers, genomics and other omics, and medical imaging — into patient-specific representations, especially intermediate fusion; (2) multimodal medical foundation models that reason across modalities; (3) LLM-based clinical reasoning for diagnosis, treatment planning and predicting the best treatment for an individual patient; (4) chain-of-thought and other methods that make cross-modal clinical reasoning transparent and interpretable for physicians; (5) translation into real clinical workflows — clinical agents, documentation burden, human oversight, external validation. Less interested in single-modality benchmark increments, off-the-shelf models applied to small private datasets without new insight, and molecular or drug-discovery work with no patient-level angle.",
